---
import HomeLayout from '@/components/layout/HomeLayout.astro';
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from '@/components/ui/card';
import { ScrollArea } from '@/components/ui/scroll-area';

const link = 'text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-500';
---

<HomeLayout>
  <div class="flex-grow container mx-auto py-6 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <Card className="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <CardHeader>
        <CardTitle className="text-3xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</CardTitle>
      </CardHeader>
      <CardContent>
        <ScrollArea client:load className="h-[calc(100vh-16rem)] pr-4">
          <section class="space-y-6">
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Cliplink is a URL shortener run by Oswaldo Osuna. This page lists
              what Cliplink stores, why, and where.
            </p>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">1. What Cliplink stores</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground">
              <li>
                If you sign in: your name, email address, and avatar, as shared
                by Google or GitHub, and which of the two you signed in with.
                Signing in with both using the same verified email gives you one
                User.
              </li>
              <li>
                For every Link: its Destination, its Code, its Name if you gave
                it one, and its Owner if you were signed in. A Link created
                without signing in has no Owner.
              </li>
              <li>
                Sessions: a record in the database and a cookie in your browser
                that keep you signed in until you sign out or the session
                expires.
              </li>
            </ul>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">2. Analytics</h2>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Cliplink uses Vercel Analytics to count page views and Vercel
              Speed Insights to measure how fast pages load. These are reported
              in aggregate and are not tied to your User.
            </p>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">3. Rate limiting</h2>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Vercel's firewall limits how many requests one IP address can
              make, to stop abuse. Cliplink itself does not store your IP
              address.
            </p>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">4. Where it lives</h2>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Cliplink runs on Vercel and keeps its data in a Postgres database
              on Neon. Your data is not sold or shared with anyone else.
            </p>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">5. Deleting your data</h2>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              You can delete any Link you own. You can also delete your User:
              this removes your name, email address, avatar, sign-in links to
              Google and GitHub, and sessions, and every Link you own becomes a
              Deleted Link. A Deleted Link no longer leads anywhere, but its
              Code stays reserved so it is never given to anyone else. Links
              created without signing in have no Owner, so they can't be deleted
              this way.
            </p>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">6. Google and GitHub</h2>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              When you sign in, Google or GitHub handles your sign-in under its
              own privacy policy:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground">
              <li>
                <a
                  class={link}
                  href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                >
                  Google Privacy Policy
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a
                  class={link}
                  href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                >
                  GitHub General Privacy Statement
                </a>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">7. Contact</h2>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Questions about this policy go to{' '}
              <a class={link} href="mailto:oswaldo.adrian35@gmail.com">
                oswaldo.adrian35@gmail.com
              </a>
              .
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-8">
              Last updated: November 2026
            </p>
          </section>
        </ScrollArea>
      </CardContent>
    </Card>
  </div>
</HomeLayout>
